  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>compan</keyword>
  <short_description>Companion matrix.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>A = compan(c)</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input>
    <param_input_item>
      <param_name>c</param_name>
      <param_description>a vector of polynomial coefficients, in descending powers.</param_description>
    </param_input_item>
  </param_input>
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>A</param_name>
      <param_description>the companion matrix whose first row is <b>-c(2:end) / c(1)</b> and whose first subdiagonal is ones.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p><b>compan</b> returns the companion matrix of the polynomial whose coefficients are <b>c</b>.</p>
    <p>The eigenvalues of the companion matrix are the roots of the polynomial, so <b>eig(compan(c))</b> and <b>roots(c)</b> return the same values.</p>
    <p>For a vector of length n, the result is an (n-1)-by-(n-1) matrix. A single coefficient returns an empty matrix.</p>
  </description>
  <used_function />
  <bibliography />
  <examples>
    <example_item>
      <example_item_type>nelson</example_item_type>
      <example_item_description />
      <example_item_data runnable="cli"><![CDATA[A = compan([1 -6 11 -6])
r = eig(A)
]]></example_item_data>
    </example_item>
  </examples>
